ns at the level of president van  der lion  commissioner simpson executive vice  president tim runs higher ups and high  representative vice president borrel and  of course and throughout all our  services so yeah we are we are looking  to to diversify our sources uh that's  that's something we've been working on  for uh for several months uh already  going back as far as  last summer last autumn when we noted  the price is increasing due to due to  the supply squeeze in the global market  and that's the situation which has been  exacerbated  by the current  situation  in ukraine and that's why we continue to  pursue these talks  okay i see no further questions on  energy so we move to other topics yes  thank you it's it's a question regarding  crisis management  after yesterday um  just so sorry  thanks  so my question is that yesterday the  commission proposed measures to sort of  soften the blow of rising energy  prices according to researchers we're  going to see  a rise in  in a likely rise in food prices as well  that may be as high as  20 to 50 percent is that something the  commission is looking into at the moment  uh or can you see similar programs be  sort of called to call for for sorry  um  uh to start a hearing process on similar  uh proposals with regarding to combat  food prices  thanks sorry yeah thank you very much um  well of course the commission is  monitoring the overall economic  situation very very closely  based on  the impact that the invasion of ukraine  has  uh to go to the example that you have  mentioned which is indeed an extremely  important one it's clear as well that  there is a link to  the rise in energy prices because  obviously  energy is an important input into the  production of foodstuffs  be it because you need fuel for tractors  be it because the production of  fertilizers requires energy  etc etc so this is something which the  commission is um is tracking um very  closely um and of course  we will if need be come forward u